  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e74248e54e324e3e277d6c53f7cca2f9cc6f0323c36fbe4a45dabd10cebfd55d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e74248e54e32-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia: \u201cBut you want to go beyond constructive discovery?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e74248e54e324e3e277d6c53f7cca2f9cc6f0323c36fbe4a45dabd10cebfd55d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e74248e54e32-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia: \u201cNow, you are telling me that there was no choice between the two\u2026 what were we doing in Lampf, spinning our wheels?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e74248e54e324e3e277d6c53f7cca2f9cc6f0323c36fbe4a45dabd10cebfd55d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e74248e54e32-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor: \u201cCould you tell me what the difference is between actual knowledge and constructive knowledge?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e74248e54e324e3e277d6c53f7cca2f9cc6f0323c36fbe4a45dabd10cebfd55d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e74248e54e32-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, justice Alito: \u201cIf actual knowledge means things that the plaintiff doesn't actually know, then I don't know what the difference is between actual knowledge and constructive knowledge. It's a meaningless distinction.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e74248e54e324e3e277d6c53f7cca2f9cc6f0323c36fbe4a45dabd10cebfd55d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e74248e54e32-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer: \u201cSo how\u2014what\u2019s the right phrasing? \u2026 does the statute begin to run when a reasonable person would have found facts sufficient to show a violation?\u201d"
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Oral Argument",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e74248e54e324e3e277d6c53f7cca2f9cc6f0323c36fbe4a45dabd10cebfd55d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e74248e54e32-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, the case concerns whether the statute of limitations for private securities fraud claims is governed by the discovery rule, which starts the clock when the plaintiff discovers the facts constituting the violation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "David C. Frederick",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e74248e54e324e3e277d6c53f7cca2f9cc6f0323c36fbe4a45dabd10cebfd55d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e74248e54e32-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to David C. Frederick, petitioners argue that Congress intended the term \u201cdiscovery\u201d in the securities fraud statute to have its ordinary meaning."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "David C. Frederick",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e74248e54e324e3e277d6c53f7cca2f9cc6f0323c36fbe4a45dabd10cebfd55d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e74248e54e32-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 29,
              "start": 29
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to David C. Frederick, petitioners also contend that they would prevail under either an actual\u2011knowledge or constructive\u2011knowledge standard."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "David C. Frederick",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e74248e54e324e3e277d6c53f7cca2f9cc6f0323c36fbe4a45dabd10cebfd55d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e74248e54e32-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 32,
              "start": 32
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to David C. Frederick, petitioners note that Congress included a five\u2011year repose period in the statute."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e74248e54e324e3e277d6c53f7cca2f9cc6f0323c36fbe4a45dabd10cebfd55d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e74248e54e32-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 1,
              "start": 1
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "An amicus curiae filed on behalf of the respondents."
      }
    ],
